# Accepted-paper profile: method

- Sample: `sample.json` — 15 NeurIPS main-track papers (2024: 7, 2025: 8) chosen by title from the proceedings indexes (https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2024 and `/2025/vol38-main-conference`) for the audience of this study (evaluation of language models, efficient/label-efficient evaluation, prediction-powered and active inference for evaluation, performance prediction). Being in these proceedings is the evidence of acceptance. The paper of the task's starter list item 6 (NeurIPS 2025) is deliberately not in the sample (the study uses it for data/code only).
- PDFs are the camera-ready `*-Paper-Conference.pdf` from the proceedings; text by `pdftotext -layout` (poppler). Not committed (third-party files).
- `count_captions_refs.py`: finds the first `References` heading, takes everything before it as main text, lists `Figure N`/`Table N` captions there. Gaps in numbering (side-by-side figures the regex misses) were resolved by hand by locating the missing caption's page (all were in the main text, except in the 553-page file of Observational Scaling Laws, which has an anomalous layout and is excluded: 14 papers are analysed). Reference counts: the PDF list for papers with `[n]`-style or author-year entries, checked against Semantic Scholar `referenceCount` (`sample.json`); where they disagree the figure that matches the printed list is used.
- Limits: purposive sample, not random; camera-ready versions (10 pages, one more than submission); counts of captions are of captioned items, so a multi-panel figure is one figure.
